{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee. I understand you’re here for abdominal pain. I know you’re feeling sleepy from the Dilaudid, but I’ll speak clearly so you can lip-read. Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. I’m sorry I’m so tired. The pain was really bad last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No need to apologize. Your husband told me the pain is in your upper belly, constant, like your past episodes. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, right here — epigastric. It’s familiar. I haven’t been eating much because it hurts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you’ve been nauseous, but no vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just nausea. I didn’t take much of my oral Dilaudid at home — I was afraid it would make me sicker."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ve checked your labs. Your lipase is mildly elevated — 103 — which supports mild pancreatitis. But your liver tests and other labs are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s pancreatitis again? Like last time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely acute on chronic, probably due to your sphincter of Oddi dysfunction. But this episode seems mild. No fever, and your vitals are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need another ERCP?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We consulted GI. Since your liver enzymes are normal and you’re improving, they don’t think you need another ERCP this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried about more procedures."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you IV fluids for now and let your bowel rest a bit. You’ll stay on your regular pain meds as needed, but we’ll watch that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve had low blood pressure before when I’m nauseous. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring that. Your blood pressure is stable now — around 98 over 65. We’ll keep you on maintenance fluids to help prevent drops."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my anxiety’s been worse lately. PTSD stuff. Is it okay to keep taking my clonazepam?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, absolutely. We’ll continue all your home medications, including fluoxetine, prazosin, and your sleep meds. We want you to feel safe and comfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I also get constipated in the hospital. Last time it was really bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on your usual bowel regimen — docusate and senna — to prevent that. I felt some fullness on exam, so we need to stay ahead of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2155-06-15 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. That helps a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2155-06-15 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Just checking in. How’s the pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2155-06-15 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I took 2 mg Dilaudid an hour ago. Pain’s down to a 3. Still nauseous, but not vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2155-06-15 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good progress. We’ll keep encouraging fluids and may try a light diet later if you’re up for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2155-06-15 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d like to try a little food. Maybe toast?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2155-06-15 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with clear liquids first — broth or apple juice — and see how you do. If that goes well, we’ll advance to a full diet tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2155-06-15 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I understand. Thank you for explaining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2155-06-15 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. You kept down the broth and juice. Any pain or nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2155-06-15 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No nausea now. Pain is mild — I didn’t need more pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2155-06-15 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. We’ll switch you to a regular diet for dinner. That’s a big step toward going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2155-06-15 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? I might go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2155-06-15 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you keep this up, yes. You’re stable, pain is controlled, and labs look good. We’ll see how you do with food and plan for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2155-06-15 14:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. I was worried it would take longer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2155-06-15 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Evening check-in. You ate most of your dinner and feel okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2155-06-15 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, no problems. I took my evening meds — senna, docusate, trazodone. I think I’ll sleep well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2155-06-15 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll continue the ranitidine for stomach protection and heparin to prevent clots while you’re here. All part of routine care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2155-06-15 18:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. Makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2155-06-16 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re officially ready to go home. You’ve had a regular breakfast, no pain, no nausea. Vitals are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2155-06-16 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great news. What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2155-06-16 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If pain worsens, you vomit, or develop a fever, call your GI doctor or go to the ER. Otherwise, keep taking your meds, stay hydrated, and follow up with your GI and primary care providers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2155-06-16 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my hearing — should I mention anything to my doctors?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2155-06-16 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, always let providers know you’re deaf and lip-read. We’ve noted it in your chart. Your husband can help if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2155-06-16 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for taking the time to talk clearly. I felt respected and heard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2155-06-16 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Take care of yourself. We’ll see you only if you need us — otherwise, stay well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2155-06-16 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2155-06-15 07:55:00",
    "admission_end": "2155-06-16 13:05:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of chronic pancreatitis and sphincter of Oddi dysfunction was admitted for recurrent epigastric abdominal pain and nausea. She presented with poor oral intake and was managed with IV fluids, bowel rest, and continuation of her home pain and anxiety medications. Her lipase was mildly elevated at 103, consistent with mild acute pancreatitis, but she improved quickly without need for ERCP. She tolerated a regular diet, remained hemodynamically stable, and had no complications. Constipation was anticipated and managed with her usual bowel regimen. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to follow up with her GI and primary care providers and to monitor for worsening symptoms.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute pancreatitis",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Other specified disorders of biliary tract",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Unspecified hearing loss",
      "Family history of malignant neoplasm of breast",
      "Constipation, unspecified",
      "Need for prophylactic vaccination and inoculation against influenza"
    ]
  }
}
